<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as OPEC, Organisation of the Petroleum Exporting Countries</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC) is an intergovernmental organisation of oil-producing states founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in September 1960 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, Kuwait, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and Venezuela. It coordinates its members' petroleum policies, chiefly through production quotas. The price rises of 1973–1974 shifted power in the world oil market from Western companies to producing governments. Its headquarters are in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/opec.jpg" alt="Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_OPEC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
